[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186221420 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-047ba9d9-f028-5122-88f6-0f2794537abb" "question-2812ec6f-62e9-58a6-b999-e2e9bb1ef20a" "question-808ef5db-aeee-5e2b-ba0b-cf24a0046d0e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-047ba9d9-f028-5122-88f6-0f2794537abb" :question/id #uuid "047ba9d9-f028-5122-88f6-0f2794537abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-334280" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental matrix could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9da6b88c-3427-5d82-9c0a-0c12e0c3ee52"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9da6b88c-3427-5d82-9c0a-0c12e0c3ee52" :answer-field/id #uuid "9da6b88c-3427-5d82-9c0a-0c12e0c3ee52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-86fef8d9-8391-5f43-a431-4aca16a969d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b87a16e-5a64-5611-ba3d-ad9a201c30bc" "answer-783bf694-f05d-5263-9612-4fd18e3c4b45" "answer-86fef8d9-8391-5f43-a431-4aca16a969d0" "answer-a312ecaa-05e8-5874-ba6e-ea1c4899eeed" "answer-6dacf3f0-1719-5079-8d03-5335eb4e6a3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b87a16e-5a64-5611-ba3d-ad9a201c30bc" :answer/id #uuid "2b87a16e-5a64-5611-ba3d-ad9a201c30bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-783bf694-f05d-5263-9612-4fd18e3c4b45" :answer/id #uuid "783bf694-f05d-5263-9612-4fd18e3c4b45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86fef8d9-8391-5f43-a431-4aca16a969d0" :answer/id #uuid "86fef8d9-8391-5f43-a431-4aca16a969d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t} & {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a312ecaa-05e8-5874-ba6e-ea1c4899eeed" :answer/id #uuid "a312ecaa-05e8-5874-ba6e-ea1c4899eeed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dacf3f0-1719-5079-8d03-5335eb4e6a3c" :answer/id #uuid "6dacf3f0-1719-5079-8d03-5335eb4e6a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3} & 2e \\\\ -2{e}^{3} & e\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2812ec6f-62e9-58a6-b999-e2e9bb1ef20a" :question/id #uuid "2812ec6f-62e9-58a6-b999-e2e9bb1ef20a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334287" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} \\\\ -{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 3{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} & {e}^{5t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & 3{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7e1c8270-c94c-5afb-bb4e-783c3deb13c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7e1c8270-c94c-5afb-bb4e-783c3deb13c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e1c8270-c94c-5afb-bb4e-783c3deb13c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c012ce1d-eb1d-5b42-88cb-96ac6a6d3311" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be97f123-ee31-529e-ad62-b60cd32f0447" "answer-a0f3c51e-4158-53a9-8000-4d759b58f125" "answer-5b9538e4-7f8a-5b8c-82bb-35b03e432d62" "answer-c012ce1d-eb1d-5b42-88cb-96ac6a6d3311" "answer-a33d5d0e-3557-5992-9c38-968bde775fc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be97f123-ee31-529e-ad62-b60cd32f0447" :answer/id #uuid "be97f123-ee31-529e-ad62-b60cd32f0447" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0f3c51e-4158-53a9-8000-4d759b58f125" :answer/id #uuid "a0f3c51e-4158-53a9-8000-4d759b58f125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2e & {e}^{5} \\\\ -e & 3{e}^{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b9538e4-7f8a-5b8c-82bb-35b03e432d62" :answer/id #uuid "5b9538e4-7f8a-5b8c-82bb-35b03e432d62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} & 3{e}^{5t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & {e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c012ce1d-eb1d-5b42-88cb-96ac6a6d3311" :answer/id #uuid "c012ce1d-eb1d-5b42-88cb-96ac6a6d3311" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} & {e}^{5t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & 3{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a33d5d0e-3557-5992-9c38-968bde775fc4" :answer/id #uuid "a33d5d0e-3557-5992-9c38-968bde775fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-808ef5db-aeee-5e2b-ba0b-cf24a0046d0e" :question/id #uuid "808ef5db-aeee-5e2b-ba0b-cf24a0046d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-334308" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t+2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}t+2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}=[\\begin{aligned}(t+2){e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & (t+2){e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8483fff-76a3-580a-a83e-5302b7c416d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8483fff-76a3-580a-a83e-5302b7c416d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8483fff-76a3-580a-a83e-5302b7c416d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e16debc0-ce3c-5f96-873e-38c12a03e8c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-72ffadc4-335c-55d0-bd36-1d3163db7d26" "answer-81e20a17-4b6b-5eb7-b397-570b9f0dd097" "answer-156d4f34-709c-5fbe-897d-5e8c2b73d56a" "answer-3947fe3e-dc6f-51d9-bcfa-9d26dd70ad67" "answer-e16debc0-ce3c-5f96-873e-38c12a03e8c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-72ffadc4-335c-55d0-bd36-1d3163db7d26" :answer/id #uuid "72ffadc4-335c-55d0-bd36-1d3163db7d26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(t+2){e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81e20a17-4b6b-5eb7-b397-570b9f0dd097" :answer/id #uuid "81e20a17-4b6b-5eb7-b397-570b9f0dd097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-156d4f34-709c-5fbe-897d-5e8c2b73d56a" :answer/id #uuid "156d4f34-709c-5fbe-897d-5e8c2b73d56a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & t+2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3947fe3e-dc6f-51d9-bcfa-9d26dd70ad67" :ans